  "note": "Bayesian evidence comparison with nested sampling (UltraNest) over the same PN+MOS1+MOS2 0.5-10 keV data used by xmm_xspec. BXA builds the prior transform from the parameter list below; constants are fixed at the chi-square best fit so models are compared under one calibration. Priors are centred on the least-squares solution and are deliberately wide. Parameter names follow the PyXspec model definitions in this image (zpowerlw.Redshift, zgauss.Redshift, zxipcf.Nh/log_xi/CvrFract, pcfabs.CvrFract). TBabs/pcfabs/cabs/zxipcf column densities use XSPEC's 1e22 cm^-2 units. The soft-excess family (plbb*) was trialled and withdrawn: with an 11-dex blackbody normalisation prior the sampler wandered into a region where the blackbody dominates and the log-likelihood falls to ~-4e5, so no evidence from that family is quoted.  sigma(Fe K-alpha) extends to 2 keV so a broad component cannot pin at the prior boundary; the broad-line Bayes factor must therefore be read as continuum-curvature-degenerate, not as a detection. cutoffpl_cabs is unidentifiable on 0.5-10 keV PPS data (best chi2/dof 2.701 vs 2.696 for a plain power law, i.e. delta-chi2 = 2.6 for two extra parameters): its evidence is not quoted, and a Compton-thick comparison needs broadband data.",
